WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.744
Emperor Zhuangzong of Later Tang, Li Cunxu, was a young emperor who loved music and theatre.

00:00:07.094 --> 00:00:09.998
The court musicians played beside him.

00:00:10.348 --> 00:00:17.572
After taking the throne, he spent all day amusing himself with the actors around him, and left the great affairs of state to them.

00:00:17.922 --> 00:00:20.874
The actors wore splendid stage costumes.

00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:28.232
The actors meddled in court affairs; he would not listen to his loyal officials, and the court grew more chaotic day by day.

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:36.622
Within a few years a mutiny broke out; Zhuangzong died in the chaos, and Later Tang headed for its end.

00:00:36.972 --> 00:00:40.788
Under the setting sun, the palace was silent.

00:00:41.138 --> 00:00:49.226
Later, the Song dynasty writer Ouyang Xiu wrote the 'Preface to the Biographies of the Court Actors', telling this history.

00:00:49.576 --> 00:00:57.184
This story tells people: worry and toil can make a country flourish, while ease and pleasure can bring ruin.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:00.966
Sunlight filled the palace courtyard.

